7805b0a6-b84a-4830-b45c-0333716313b4	be494cdb-6742-405b-9a47-60c329c96356	7461fbc3-1623-4068-8423-df2c348212f0	The strategy exhibits a "fair-weather" profile, performing reasonably well in normal market conditions but failing catastrophically during the COVID stress period. It is not robust to market shocks, as shown by the severe negative returns and large drawdown during the high-volatility regime. The extremely low number of trades across both periods makes these results statistically insignificant and highly questionable for predicting future performance.	The provided performance data does not contain the specific sentiment words or headlines that triggered trades. Therefore, it is impossible to identify which patterns led to profitable trades or false-positives.	The strategy's failure during the COVID regime was caused by its inability to handle a high-volatility, sustained market crash. The model was likely optimized for the mean-reverting conditions of a normal market and was unprepared for the velocity of the sell-off. This probably led to false sentiment triggers, such as buying dips prematurely based on extreme fear signals, resulting in repeated losses and a significant drawdown as the market continued to fall.	[0.010091578,0.04110949,-0.020049851,-0.00045385165,-0.011036363,0.032363586,-0.014764486,0.001254772,0.00223025,-0.11261832,-0.01850593,0.04930346,0.009015296,0.0024279407,-0.0035671822,0.006942242,0.03454972,-0.03546401,0.010138316,0.014270931,-0.017254582,0.017751463,-0.011946653,0.034185,0.0050931787,0.012621844,0.0047254763,-0.009781781,0.016631357,0.23533656,-0.013208511,-0.05041321,0.010064906,-0.009996019,-0.040968865,0.011465284,0.009492218,0.028367959,0.035544164,0.017532708,0.026038444,0.030448547,0.015834048,0.038917255,0.03685662,-0.03710423,-0.021431874,0.030904775,-0.019719206,-0.024553953,-0.0056851306,-0.003067071,0.01875417,-0.008318989,0.02563109,0.031609345,0.0068421667,0.0029290058,0.039529614,-0.0020606169,-0.033082254,0.02370